msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:62
#: 2b6cf0c8d6ed44c29c1dc34663428103
msgid "Connecting the Sonar Sensor on APM 2.x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:64
#: 147ba05cfdaf438d979a52438843aaac
msgid "The sensor's GND, V+ and \"AN\" or \"3\" pins should be connected to APM 2's A0 pins as shown in the diagram below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:71
#: 457071ce5c6342fda3171543242fc2de
msgid "Connecting the Sonar Sensor on PX4FMU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:73
#: 9addff4f4b6d4301bdf94ee127d9a9fc
msgid "You will need to assign the Sonar (signal line) to an appropriate PX4 pin in Mission Planner - Configuration - Advanced Params - Adv Parameter List using the SONAR_PIN parameter.  The following PX4 \"Pins\" are available for SONAR use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:77
#: 38b989d23f374c3e963cef772f4050cd
msgid "SONAR_PIN = 11 - (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:79
#: 74f1ce22230f492f914a19cc39e3a1a0
msgid "The \"airspeed\" pin. Located on a 3 pin DF13 connector on the PX4IO board, but directly visible to the ADC on the PX4FMU. This pin can take voltages up to 6.6V (it has an internal voltage divider)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:82
#: d489f7327e2643f6a66d96ec952b18da
msgid "SONAR_PIN = 12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:84
#: 983b5cde7c0347109c4844f381683ee0
msgid "A general analog input pin. Located on pin 3 of the \"FMUSPI\" port on the PX4IO board, this pin is directly visible to the PX4FMU analog input code. This can take voltages up to 3.3V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:88
#: 63554d68572f41ef816bfcaecb264bee
msgid "SONAR_PIN = 13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:90
#: 0bdc1d6cbeed4ed78a4775c154a5f25c
msgid "A general analog input pin. Located on pin 4 of the \"FMUSPI\" port on the PX4IO board, this pin is directly visible to the PX4FMU analog input code. This can take voltages up to 3.3V.  It is being worked on and will be included in this section when it is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:96
#: d1ec6381655a4cd8b27ae429866d2c20
msgid "Mounting the Sonar Sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:98
#: 7800a9bbd8d34866bb6d256d83934ad2
msgid "It's important that the sonar sensor be mounted at least three inches (10cm) away from sources of electrical noise including the ESCs and other interference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:102
#: 1c9b7f87edc14ac1a1205479a0e62574
msgid "Enabling the Sonar through Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:104
#: 8cee188f06fa4437b4ea9581141bb70a
msgid "Enable the sonar by connecting your APM/PX4 to the Mission Planner and then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:106
#: d9c57a2bf77a46c19f4be3da6b83b6d3
msgid "Go to Initial Setup > Optional Hardware > Sonar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:107
#: 744c2f7366d54970bdf7d575acf65dd5
msgid "Check the \"Enable\" checkbox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:108
#: a6209986ba004713b49ecc6418d88b80
msgid "Select the sonar model from the drop down list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:114
#: ad34764e9dfa492cb605f720d0f14465
msgid "Testing the sonar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:116
#: a380ac43b2fb4b1a9eeea481622eff51
msgid "You can test the sonar basically works by connecting your APM/PX4 to the mission planner and then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:119
#: 0a4f97a536fa499ca88f6f860937d068
msgid "Go to the Terminal window and press \"Connect to APM\" or \"Connect to PX4\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:120
#: a84b2365cd4949d0b1cc6ee41e4adcda
msgid "when the prompt appears type *test*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:121
#: 9e42970a32d148a7afd6c8c090d5cda1
msgid "type *sonar*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:123
#: 4355bc8a6a5c4e01986ca7dccae60355
msgid "The current distanced sensed by the sonar should be displayed.  Aim the sonar at targets of different distances (i.e. ceiling, wall, etc) and ensure the numbers change.  If they do not then there may be a hardware issue with the sonar or cabling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:128
#: 8176c61fc81c46e988330a5701ce3fe3
msgid "You should also hear the sonar clicking very rapidly (10hz) whenever power is applied if you do not hear this then it's possible that the sonar is defective or is not being powered for some reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:133
#: aa384128f32d4e5f82b0d8c6a1164a67
msgid "Tuning the gain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:135
#: 08a1a143d5564743a1e78290ff81aee4
msgid "If when flying you find that your copter bobs up and down it is possible that the default SONAR_GAIN is too high for your copter.  Go to the mission planner's Config/Tuning > Full Parameter List and reduce the SONAR_GAIN parameter from its default of 0.2 to 0.1 or even 0.05 and press \"Write Params\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:142
#: 1a4b68e60b734225abd7f0bc1e4c5211
msgid "Sonar Maximum Altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:144
#: 2352f997566345d798589d77d400bf9e
msgid "When enabled Sonar is used as the means of determining altitude below Sonar Maximum Altitude, above that the barometer is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:146
#: 86682051ce9d409a847e66159c5695e5
msgid "Sonar Maximum Altitude is calculated as 60 percent of the factory specified maximum Sonar range for the Sonar type selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:148
#: cd4380258e5f484aa6492865d6f45f95
msgid "Sonar is used for determining altitude only when the Sonar itself is detecting the ground and is below its Sonar Maximum Altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:151
#: 5ba61a102ad24a8091ce04637af9aa5d
msgid "XL-EZ4 or XL-EZ0 have a Maximum range of 7.65 meters and a Sonar Maximum Altitude of 4.59 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:153
#: 72a4b7a5b3bb4bbbb702c1f5f93cbbea
msgid "XL-EZLO have a Maximum range of 10.68 meters and a Sonar Maximum Altitude = 6.4 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:155
#: 6fbcea2745694ec6be2e01afa537c9d5
msgid "HRLV-EZ4 or HRLV-EZ0 with Maximum range of 5 meters and a Sonar Maximum Altitude of 3 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:157
#: ab1484287344468fa1f30b1fe3a32754
msgid "LV-EZ4 or LV-EZ0 have a Maximum range of 6.45 meters and a Sonar Maximum Altitude = 3.87 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:160
#: d8e92d1f28fa4301a171fffc3830ad6d
msgid "If the Sonar gets an unreliable return below the Sonar Maximum Altitude, it is ignored and the Barometer altitude is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:164
#: d80c2e4179524bdc9418e6ffa23ce865
msgid "Cold weather performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:166
#: b88fefbcf98e4a09b65a3480b6b25ce5
msgid "The :ref:`MaxBotix <common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog>` XL-EZ0 sonar (and other variations of their indoor sonar) may not function for about 10 minutes after an extreme drop in temperature (i.e. a drop from a warm 27C/80F house to the chilly 10C/50F outdoors) because of condensation building up on the sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:172
#: 8ca98a61cb944783a8968713e888c073
msgid "`This post <https://diydrones.com/forum/topics/arducopter-2-0-48?xg_source=activity&id=705844%3ATopic%3A676942&page=31#comments>`__ includes one member's (`Geir Engebakken <https://www.diydrones.com/forum/topic/listForContributor?user=3a28calx54gma>`__) solution (initially suggested by the developer Olivier ADLER) involving attaching 4x10Ohm resistors to the base of the sonar powered from a 5V source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:179
#: 7036f21483dc46c3ac4461910f654510
msgid "Other Potential Causes of Sonar Noise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:181
#: fbd8d90c6e994426b56aad82b3db3dff
msgid "If you are having problems with excessive noise on your sonar as shown in the dataflash log below (sonar is in red, baro is in green)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:187
#: db957ca4a1b0483e9fbd2dbdfbc4b710
msgid "There are a number of possible causes which should be investigated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:189
#: 25c669f1ef844013a298d615c30b79e4
msgid "Sonar is susceptible to \"noise\" from a variety of sources and several \"fixes\" may be required to achieve adequate performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:192
#: 7429f3ec9a5e423cb28698e2b910bdf6
msgid "Electrical noise caused by ESCs, Servos, or switching BEC's on the same circuit as the Sonar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:195
#: 8446b20a1aeb4c1f81abfa6090c8370a
msgid "The RC filter and use of shielded cable as described above are usually sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:198
#: 0e970b8aea19455ea70cd759dc12d477
msgid "EMF radiation from motors, motor wires, ESC's or Xbee."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:200
#: 6c86b7860f5a45f788a7153e9960c640
msgid "Sonar is especially susceptible to AC EMF noise generated by the ESCs and ESC to motor wiring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:202
#: bd19cf6a75ab4da3872166739a13b8a2
msgid "This can be greatly reduced by wrapping the nearby ESCs and their motor wiring in aluminum (gutter) tape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:205
#: 596f1de272344da18a288dca4138461b
msgid "Acoustic noise from propellers, prop wash and turbulence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:207
#: 1405e1ce39c24e69a3d0f86961d8f513
msgid "It is very important to keep the Sonar out of direct prop wash or turbulence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:209
#: 585892dbb0834c42b25354355bf60954
msgid "Balancing propellers (and motors) can help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:210
#: 389cc7af6d5c49e2a8cb7a11590d420f
msgid "Mounting the sonar sensor inside a small can or tube thinly lined with foam can greatly reduce unwanted exterior acoustic noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:212
#: 088d4e09de8e4bd2b7816017fdc8a107
msgid "Wrap Sonar module board and components in rubber or foam tape to reduce transferred acoustic noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:215
#: eb432d4bcd66488cbba13f876bf223f9
msgid "Vibration from motors, props, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:217
#: ee44fb45bbd642fb8a0d14a25ab3374f
msgid "Sonar is very subject to frame transmitted vibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:218
#: de864582b0024af9a2dc087486893b5d
msgid "Mounting the Sonar module on double sided foam or Gel tape will pretty much eliminate this noise source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:221
#: f4f853bae73845cba51522d588ec8695
msgid "The MB 1240 series is the only Sonar considered suitable for multicopter use by the manufacturer - Maxbotix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:226
#: d147a001c0e84f4897e3eb8b04b569b8
msgid "Please read this tutorial for a comprehensive review: `Interfacing an Ultrasonic Sensor with a Pixhawk or ArduPilot Mega <https://www.maxbotix.com/articles/ultrasonic-sensors-pixhawk-ardupilot.htm>`__."
msgstr ""
